      "defect": "unlicensed-inference",
      "evidence": "The proof says: “The cutoffs are nondecreasing. Minimality of $q$ therefore gives $m_{r-1}<m_r$ for $2\\le r\\le q$.” Nondecreasing cutoffs and minimality of the first cutoff equal to $t$ do not by themselves imply strict increase before $q$; a nondecreasing sequence may plateau below $t$. Strictness does follow quickly from the displayed cutoff formula and $\\sqrt\\ell\\ge2$, but that needed argument is absent.",
