      "defect": "unlicensed-inference",
      "evidence": "Step 1.1 infers that the pair is pure merely because “[F1] says every vertex of $A^k_{j_k}\\subseteq B_k$ is pure to $A^i_{j_i}$.” Vertexwise purity in that one direction does not itself make the two sets a pure pair: some vertices of $A^k_{j_k}$ could be complete to $A^i_{j_i}$ and others anticomplete. The conclusion is recoverable by also applying [F1] with $i,k$ reversed (and using nonemptiness), which forces a uniform relation, but the written inference does not supply that argument.",
